{
  "path": "lua/ge/extensions/editor/util/editorElementHelper.lua",
  "module": "Editor helper that builds imgui forms driven by declared \"elements\" (numeric, text, boolean, 3D transform, vehicle model/config, file, race, sites, ranking, dropdown, vehicle filter, zone selector, decorations...). Used mostly by the mission/quest/test editor: a derived class declares its elements in init(), then you call setContainer(c) to load the values, draw() to display/edit, getNewData() to get the default values and checkContainer() to detect missing or mistyped fields. The module returns a constructor: require('/lua/ge/extensions/editor/util/editorElementHelper')(derivedClass, mode); the keys of derivedClass are copied into the object.",
  "usage": "local helper = require('/lua/ge/extensions/editor/util/editorElementHelper')({\n  init = function(self)\n    self:addNumeric('Durée', 'duration', 60)\n    self:addBool('Actif', 'enabled', true)\n  end\n}, 'mission')\nhelper:setContainer(mission) -- reads mission.missionTypeData\nhelper:draw()",
  "notes": [
    "The mode determines the container's data field: 'quest' -> questTypeData, 'test' -> test, otherwise missionTypeData.",
    "Each element gets a unique _id (module counter); displayOptions.associatedStars as a string is converted to a table {key = true}.",
    "Transform: writes three fields <fieldName>Pos, <fieldName>Rot, <fieldName>Scl (vec3/quat converted to tables). Model/config: <fieldName>Model, Config, ConfigPath. Ranking: <fieldName>Count, BestResult, MediumResult, WorstResult. Zone selector: <fieldName>_initialZones and _destinationZones.",
    "addFile warns if the .prefab extension is used instead of .prefab.json.",
    "Code bugs: in newDataFunctions, reward and simpleLapConfig equal the nonexistent variable `defaultValue` (nil), so these elements produce no default data; defaultColors.default/orange/red use ImVec4 with 5 arguments (1,0.6,0,8,0.75) instead of 4; elementIdSetContainer reads ctd.value instead of ctd[e.fieldName]; checkContainerFunctions.elementId points to elementIdSetContainer.",
    "editingAnyTransform also consults extensions.editor_missionEditor.getStartTriggerWindow(), which ties this helper to the mission editor."
  ],
